====================================================================================================
 POWER: N_total (matched outer-shell, infall-tagged, undisrupted diffuse members) for 3 sigma vs MG=0
====================================================================================================
  Delta_obs = D(1-eps)*f, D=0.4, eps_int=0.1; noise = quadrature(e_meas, s_FJ)

  scenario                                         |     floor f=6% |  fiducial f=10% |    kernel f=13%
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2026 published UDG/dSph (LEWIS/KCWI, 20-40%)     |            8681 |            3125 |            1850
  deep MUSE/KCWI campaign (~3 km/s on 15)          |            4823 |            1737 |            1028
  ELT resolved-star (~1.5 km/s on 15)              |            2508 |             903 |             535
  ELT + tight FJ control (s_FJ=0.08)               |            1266 |             456 |             270
  measurement-only idealization (banked)           |             772 |             278 |             165

  READ (both ways):
   * The banked 'N~100-180 vs MG at ELT precision' is recovered ONLY in the measurement-only
     idealization at the upper kernel band (f=13%: N~165; drop eps_int too -> N~134).
     The fiducial f=10% idealization is N~278. Adding the honest Faber-Jackson intrinsic-
     scatter floor s_FJ~0.15 raises the fiducial ELT requirement to N~903; the best realistic
     corner (f=13%, tight FJ control) is N~270. So the banked N was OPTIMISTIC by ~x2-5:
     the intrinsic M-sigma scatter, not instrument error, is the binding noise once ELT exists.
   * Proxy dilution fork: D=0.3 -> N x 1.8; D=0.6 (DESI-era caustic+PPS tagging on
     >200-member clusters) -> N x 0.45 relative to fiducial.
